  "notes": [
    "Chaos run: Every request to the first worker is answered 500 mock_failure. A 500 is not retried today; the clients see it.",
    "What this embedded mock cluster cannot show here: Whether a 500 would be ejected by a ratio rule (Phase 15 D4): on master nothing reacts to it, which is the baseline.",
    "Windows follow when the fault was really applied and cleared. Gateway counters (attempts per request, retries) are read at the tick that opens and closes a window (every 1s), so an attempt of a request in flight at a boundary falls in the next window; the per-request figures come from the clients.",
    "Closed-loop clients: 14 for the whole run on 32 request slots (24 left serving). Closed-loop clients wait for each response, so a failing worker also slows the offered load.",
    "Load average (1, 5 and 15 minutes) at the start of the run: 5.28 5.06 4.46; at the end: 5.09 5.03 4.48."
